    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Restlessness and inability to sit still for five days. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. van Gogh called the coordinated specialty care team and was seen the same day. Two weeks ago his aripiprazole was increased from 10 to 15 mg because he still heard his name called as he fell asleep. Since then the night-time voices have stopped, but for five days he has felt an inner restlessness he cannot switch off. He cannot sit at his easel for more than a few minutes, paces his studio, shifts his legs when sitting, and lies awake because his legs will not keep still. The feeling is worst in the late afternoon, a few hours after his morning dose. He was frightened that the illness was coming back, and the restlessness makes him irritable and miserable. He has had no confusion, no voices by day, and no stiffness or tremor. He has taken naltrexone daily, has had one or two drinks on three evenings this week, and has not drunk more to calm the feeling. He has not had thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the passive thoughts of not waking up have not returned. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Five days ago, nine days after the aripiprazole increase to 15 mg</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Inner restlessness, mainly in the legs</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>Five days, constant</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>An urge to move that he cannot resist; pacing; shifting his legs while sitting</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Moderate; cannot paint or sleep through it</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>Worst in the late afternoon</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Aripiprazole increased from 10 to 15 mg two weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Walking eases it briefly; coffee makes it worse</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Poor sleep and irritability; no voices by day, confusion, stiffness, tremor, fever, or thoughts of suicide or self-harm</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Constitutional</td><td>Negative</td><td>No fever or sweats</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>Positive</td><td>Restless legs and an urge to move; no stiffness, tremor, abnormal movements of the face or tongue, or weakness</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiovascular</td><td>Negative</td><td>No palpitations, fainting, or chest pain</td></tr><tr><td>Respiratory</td><td>Negative</td><td>No wheeze or asthma</td></tr><tr><td>Psychiatric</td><td>Positive</td><td>Anxious and irritable with the restlessness; poor sleep; no voices by day; no thoughts of suicide or self-harm</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>5 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

