    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>First episode of psychosis with mood features: weeks of very little sleep, intense work and expansive plans, then acute confusion, hallucinations and suspiciousness with self-injury, and low mood since discharge. Diagnosis provisional; differential: bipolar I disorder with psychotic features, brief psychotic or schizophreniform disorder, alcohol withdrawal delirium or alcohol-induced psychotic disorder, and psychosis related to focal epilepsy. Synthetic modern episode linked to his documented first crisis</td><td>active</td><td>provisional</td>
    <td>F29</td><td>S — Synthetic modern coding of the documented first crisis. Unspecified psychosis is coded because the cause is not yet established; the retrospective diagnoses stay in the claims.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Alcohol use disorder, moderate (heavy daily wine and anise spirits before the episode); synthetic modern episode linked to his documented heavy drinking</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>F10.20</td><td>S — Synthetic modern coding of the documented drinking and its retrospective interpretation.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Self-injury to the left ear during the acute confusional episode, without suicidal intent; wound healed after surgical care in hospital</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z91.52</td><td>S — Synthetic modern coding of the documented injury; no detail of the injury is recorded.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Akathisia from aripiprazole, two weeks after the dose was increased to 15 mg; treated by returning to 10 mg and short-term propranolol; resolved</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>G25.71</td><td>S — Synthetic medication side effect; not a historical claim.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

